# Sparkle
sparkle-private-key
*.priv

# Local release secrets — NEVER commit. The keys/ folder holds the
# Developer ID .p12, the App Store Connect .p8, and a .env with the
# cert password + notary IDs. The *.p12/*.p8/.env globs are belt-and-
# suspenders in case a key file ever lands outside keys/.
keys/
*.p12
*.p8
.env

# Local build artifacts
*.app
*.dmg
appcast.xml
updates/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code local state — ignored, EXCEPT shared project skills (checked in
# so every contributor/agent gets them, e.g. .claude/skills/ship).
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/


# Vendored DuckDB static XCFramework — built by
# bin/build-duckdb-xcframework.sh, linked by the app for its raw-row archive
# (docs/duckdb-archive.md). The artifact is ~78 MB and would land in git
# history once per version bump, so it is never committed: CI rebuilds it and
# caches it by version in .github/actions/prepare-build.
#
# `Vendor/` is ignored wholesale and the two artifacts are named again below,
# because an earlier attempt narrowed this and `git add -A` immediately swept
# in an 80 MB library that then needed a history rewrite to remove.
Vendor/

Vendor/DuckDB.xcframework/
Vendor/DuckDB.xcframework.zip

# Live-render diagnostic output (bin/dev-render-live.sh).
#
# Glob, not the one default path: these renders are the REAL store — real
# project names, real account labels, real spend — and this is a public repo.
# `screenshots/live/` alone covered the default `make render-live` output and
# nothing else, so passing an outdir (`bin/dev-render-live.sh all out/`) put
# them straight in reach of the next `git add -A`. Anything named `live*`
# under screenshots/ is diagnostic and never committed; the README set is
# generated from fake data by `make screenshots`.
screenshots/live*/
